I would check the filter, because it looks like a tab or button but is a link; codegen shows the role it sees.

```ts
const row = page.getByTestId('todo-item').filter({ hasText: 'Call the bank' });
row.getByTestId('todo-title');
await row.hover();
row.getByRole('button', { name: 'Delete' });
await expect(page.getByTestId('todo-item')).toHaveCount(3);
```
I avoided nth() because it depends on row order, so adding a todo at the top would change which element is picked. Filtering on text says what I mean and survives reordering.
